## Animation and asset grammar

Character IDs are four digits with leading zeroes, stored as strings. Paths are relative and remain valid under a GitHub Pages subpath:

assets/characters/<id>/<id>_<animation>_<frame>.png

Frames start at 1. The final number is the frame index, never an attack number or an object-instance ID. Order numerically, so frame 10 follows frame 9 rather than frame 1. Use lowercase and underscores.

| Animation family | Example asset |
| --- | --- |
| Idle | 0001_idle_1.png |
| Run | 0001_run_1.png |
| Jump / fall / land | 0001_jump_1.png / 0001_fall_1.png / 0001_land_1.png |
| Hurt / airborne hurt | 0001_hurt_1.png / 0001_midair_hurt_1.png |
| Shield preparation / hold / release | 0001_prepshield_1.png / 0001_shielding_1.png / 0001_releaseshield_1.png |
| Airborne shield | 0001_midair_shielding_1.png |
| Numbered attack N | 0001_attack1_1.png through 0001_attack5_1.png |
| Airborne numbered attack N | 0001_midair_attack1_1.png through 0001_midair_attack5_1.png |
| Extra attack | 0001_extra_attack_1.png |
| Special movement / dash | 0001_mouvment_1.png |
| Attack-created object | 0001_attack1_object_1.png |
| Extra-attack-created object | 0001_extra_attack_object_1.png |

